--TEST--
An extension call that reaches the request's memory limit runs the program's `Core\Fatal::onLimit` handler, and then the request stops with a `FATAL` — `rule:packaging/a-guest-crash-throws`, `rule:errors/on-limit`
--EXTENSION--
ledger
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Shop\Ledger;

// This function runs when the request reaches a limit.
Core\Fatal::onLimit(fn (array<string> $report): void => {
    echo "onLimit ", $report['limit'], "\n";
});

// The extension keeps a copy of every string it is given until the request ends.
// Each call adds one megabyte, so a few calls reach the 8 MB limit.
string $line = Core\Str::repeat('x', 1048576);
int $calls = 0;
while ($calls < 64) {
    $calls = $calls + 1;
    string $back = Ledger::echoString($line);
}

// This line does not run. The request stops at the limit.
echo "finished ", $calls, " calls\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[limits]
memory = "8M"
--EXPECT--
onLimit memory
--EXPECT-ERROR--
FATAL: the extension used all of the memory it may use
